.TH CHIMP-LOOP 1 "2026-11" "chimp 0.6.1"
.SH NAME
chimp-loop \- play a drum kit from a MIDI controller and loop it
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B chimp-loop
.br
.B chimp-loop
.B \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B chimp-loop
plays a 16-sound drum kit from every MIDI controller on the system and records
what you play into a loop. Press Record, play, press Record again to close the
loop (or pick a length in bars and it closes on its own); press Record again to
overdub a layer, Undo to remove the last one. Quantise (1/4 to 1/32) is applied
on playback, so it can be changed or turned off after recording.
.PP
Notes 36\(en51 play sounds 1\(en16 (an LPD8 program on notes 36\(en43 plays the first
eight); any pad or button can be assigned to a sound or to a looper control.
Loops can be saved, and exported as WAV or as a standard MIDI file (General MIDI
drum notes on channel 10).
.SH KNOBS
Eight parameters, on CC 70\(en77 (the LPD8 mk2's knobs out of the box) or on any knob
or fader assigned in the window: Filter (centre off, left low-pass, right high-pass),
Delay, Echoes (delay feedback), Reverb, Swing, Pitch and Decay of the last sound played,
and Volume. Pad velocity is recorded unless Fixed velocity is on. While the LPD8 is on a
program with desktop actions (see
.BR chimpd (1)),
the looper ignores it.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Space
Record, close the loop, overdub on/off.
.TP
.B Enter
Play / stop.
.TP
.B Backspace
Undo the last layer.
.TP
.BR Delete " or " Ctrl+Backspace
Clear the loop.
.TP
.B T
Tap tempo.
.TP
.B Z X C V, A S D F, Q W E R, 1 2 3 4
Sounds 1\(en16, laid out like the pads.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/chimp/loop.json
Settings and assignments.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/chimp/loops/
Saved loops.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/chimp/kits/<name>/
Your own kits: a folder of WAVs. Files named kick, snare_1, clap, hihat_1,
open_hihat, rim, tom_1, crash, snare_2, hihat_2, tom_2, tom_3, ride, perc_1,
perc_2, perc_3 go to those slots; others fill the gaps.
.TP
.I ~/Music/Chimp/
Exports.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PIPEWIRE_LATENCY
Defaults to 256/48000 for this program, for about 11 ms from pad to sound.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR chimp (1),
.BR chimpd (1)
